{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.H3Wedderburn","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.H3Wedderburn","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.H3GramArithmetic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.wedderburn_dim_three_eq_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.wedderburn_dim_three_eq_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H3Wedderburn.lean#L84-L88","doc":"**`dim H_3(q) = 3!` matches the factorial (sorry-free).**  Records the\nWedderburn dimension equals `Nat.factorial 3`, the shape of the general\n`dim H_n(q) = n!` claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.wedderburn_dim_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.wedderburn_dim_three","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H3Wedderburn.lean#L77-L82","doc":"**`dim H_3(q) = 3! = 6` (sorry-free).**  The Wedderburn dimension of\n`H_3(q)` at a generic parameter is `Σ_{λ ⊢ 3} (f^λ)² = 1² + 2² + 1² = 6 = 3!`\n— the `n = 3` case of `dim H_n(q) = n!` (`qou-lrz1`), from the hook-length\nSYT dimensions rather than a monogenic basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.sytDim_hook_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.sytDim_hook_formula","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H3Wedderburn.lean#L65-L75","doc":"**Hook-length formula check (sorry-free).**  Each SYT dimension satisfies\n`f^λ · ∏_x h(x) = 3!`, i.e. `f^λ = 3! / ∏ h(x)` — the Frame–Robinson–Thrall\nformula, verified against the concrete hook products above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.sytDimCol3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.sytDimCol3","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H3Wedderburn.lean#L62-L63","doc":"`f^{(111)} = 3!/6 = 1` — the sign (antisymmetric) representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.sytDimHook21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.sytDimHook21","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H3Wedderburn.lean#L59-L60","doc":"`f^{(21)} = 3!/3 = 2` — the standard (2-dim) representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.sytDimRow3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.sytDimRow3","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H3Wedderburn.lean#L56-L57","doc":"`f^{(3)} = 3!/6 = 1` — the trivial (symmetric) representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.hookProd_col3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.hookProd_col3","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H3Wedderburn.lean#L49-L52","doc":"`λ = (1,1,1)` — the single column.  Hook lengths `3, 2, 1`, product `6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.hookProd_hook21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.hookProd_hook21","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H3Wedderburn.lean#L44-L47","doc":"`λ = (2,1)` — the hook.  Hook lengths `3, 1, 1`, product `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.hookProd_row3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.hookProd_row3","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H3Wedderburn.lean#L39-L42","doc":"`λ = (3)` — the single row.  Hook lengths `3, 2, 1`, product `6`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}